if he started 40 years ago.

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:49.540
- So they don't have any
technology in the studio.

00:24:49.540 --> 00:24:50.930
They refuse to have any technology,

00:24:50.930 --> 00:24:51.763
'cause of course they do.

00:24:51.763 --> 00:24:52.910
They do it all by hand.

00:24:52.910 --> 00:24:54.956
But it's like, at what point,

00:24:54.956 --> 00:24:56.870
when you are making something for so long,

00:24:56.870 --> 00:24:58.917
are you like, "Come on, fuck off.

00:24:58.917 --> 00:25:01.490
You can't finish it. Stop
now, this is a joke."

00:25:01.490 --> 00:25:02.617
- Yeah.

00:25:02.617 --> 00:25:04.080
- "Sort it out, mate.

00:25:04.080 --> 00:25:05.530
Sort your life out, come on."

00:25:06.650 --> 00:25:08.500
- There's more to life
than just this one project.

00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:10.240
- Well you know, it goes past the point

00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:13.410
where you are just
letting this consume you

00:25:13.410 --> 00:25:15.810
to a point where you're
not creating any more.

00:25:15.810 --> 00:25:16.643
It's just taking a whole...

00:25:16.643 --> 00:25:17.927
- It's just an addiction.

00:25:17.927 --> 00:25:18.760
- Yeah, yeah.

00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:20.417
This isn't healthy,

00:25:20.417 --> 00:25:21.450
and you're not gonna finish it.

00:25:21.450 --> 00:25:24.090
- At that point, no
matter what you release,

00:25:24.090 --> 00:25:26.100
is never going to be
worth the amount of hours.

00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:27.890
- Forty years of your life.

00:25:27.890 --> 00:25:29.936
- Yeah, yeah.

00:25:29.936 --> 00:25:30.769
I mean there's only a few things

00:25:30.769 --> 00:25:32.244
that are worth 40 years of your life.

00:25:32.244 --> 00:25:33.290
- Don't get me wrong, it looks amazing.

00:25:33.290 --> 00:25:35.450
But it's also very sad
hearing the story of this guy

00:25:35.450 --> 00:25:36.560
and it just takes over his life.

00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:39.040
- I mean, he must really love it.

00:25:39.040 --> 00:25:40.283
I'm sure that's an
understatement of the year.

00:25:40.283 --> 00:25:41.210
- I don't know.

00:25:41.210 --> 00:25:42.153
I feel like,

00:25:43.050 --> 00:25:44.890
I think it's an obsession.

00:25:44.890 --> 00:25:45.962
- Is it desperation?

00:25:45.962 --> 00:25:46.795
- I don't know.

00:25:46.795 --> 00:25:48.030
It's probably one of those things where

00:25:48.030 --> 00:25:50.230
it's definitely not
healthy, whatever it is.

00:25:51.150 --> 00:25:52.620
It's not like a passion.

00:25:52.620 --> 00:25:53.453
He has passion, but...

00:25:53.453 --> 00:25:54.825
- I think it's only a passion.

00:25:54.825 --> 00:25:56.580
- I think it's obsession.

00:25:56.580 --> 00:25:57.660
Obsession is different from passion.

00:25:57.660 --> 00:25:58.890
- What's the longest you guys

00:25:58.890 --> 00:26:00.616
have ever worked on a single project?

00:26:00.616 --> 00:26:01.620
I mean, 'cause you recently

00:26:01.620 --> 00:26:03.396
just uploaded your cosplay video.

00:26:03.396 --> 00:26:04.229
- Yeah.

00:26:04.229 --> 00:26:05.400
- Very good, very good.

00:26:05.400 --> 00:26:07.850
Because I remember every
few weeks or something,

00:26:07.850 --> 00:26:09.350
you'd be like, "Yeah,
I'm going to a shoot.

00:26:09.350 --> 00:26:10.340
It's the cosplay video."

00:26:10.340 --> 00:26:13.009
I swear that went on for a
fucking year or something.

00:26:13.009 --> 00:26:15.070
- Yeah, it took long time.

00:26:15.070 --> 00:26:16.470
Yeah, it's all right, it was good.

00:26:16.470 --> 00:26:18.087
It's good fun. It wasn't too long.

00:26:18.087 --> 00:26:19.140
- [Garnt] Is that the
longest thing you worked on?

00:26:19.140 --> 00:26:20.820
- Yeah, not hours put in,

00:26:20.820 --> 00:26:23.500
but as in time and number of shoots,

00:26:23.500 --> 00:26:24.956
yeah it was the most.

00:26:24.956 --> 00:26:27.550
It's fine. It wasn't too hands-on.

00:26:27.550 --> 00:26:29.150
Just kind of getting the
edit down was difficult.

00:26:29.150 --> 00:26:32.291
- What's the most you've ever
put into one project then?

00:26:32.291 --> 00:26:34.260
- Oh my gosh.

00:26:34.260 --> 00:26:35.150
- I don't know.

00:26:35.150 --> 00:26:36.885
- Okay, I'll go first then.

00:26:36.885 --> 00:26:37.858
- [Joey] Is yours the "Fate" one?

00:26:37.858 --> 00:26:38.691
- No, no, no.

00:26:38.691 --> 00:26:41.885
The most I've ever put in was,

00:26:41.885 --> 00:26:44.280
must be 10 years ago or something now,

00:26:44.280 --> 00:26:46.247
I made this Top 20 list called

00:26:46.247 --> 00:26:49.050
"The Top Coolest Anime
Characters of All Time"

00:26:49.050 --> 00:26:50.470
or something along those lines.

00:26:50.470 --> 00:26:52.850
- That sounds like a 2010 Gigguk video.

00:26:52.850 --> 00:26:54.590
- How did this take you years?

00:26:54.590 --> 00:26:58.467
- Okay, so get this. It was eight parts.

00:26:58.467 --> 00:26:59.928
- (sighs) Okay.

00:26:59.928 --> 00:27:02.390
- It was an eight-part series,

00:27:02.390 --> 00:27:03.500
because I would spend...

00:27:03.500 --> 00:27:05.100
- [Connor] Eight-part
featuring 10 characters.

00:27:05.100 --> 00:27:06.030
- No, 20 characters.

00:27:06.030 --> 00:27:06.863
- [Connor] Oh, okay.

00:27:06.863 --> 00:27:07.901
- Yeah, yeah.

00:27:07.901 --> 00:27:10.230
So every part would contain
two or three characters

00:27:10.230 --> 00:27:13.590
and each part would be at
least 15 to 20 minutes long.

00:27:13.590 --> 00:27:14.423
- [Joey] Right.

00:27:14.423 --> 00:27:17.820
- And I was working on
this one single project

00:27:17.820 --> 00:27:19.600
basically throughout university.

00:27:19.600 --> 00:27:21.110
I basically wasn't uploading anything

00:27:21.110 --> 00:27:23.007
but this one fucking series.

00:27:23.007 --> 00:27:25.560
And I realized, about two videos in,

00:27:25.560 --> 00:27:27.970
after I'd spent months
just working on two videos,

00:27:27.970 --> 00:27:30.607
I'm just like, "I've
made a massive mistake."

00:27:30.607 --> 00:27:31.440
- [Connor] Did you finish it?

00:27:31.440 --> 00:27:33.350
- I did finish it.
- [Connor] Wow.

00:27:33.350 --> 00:27:36.578
- It took me an entire year to finish.

00:27:36.578 --> 00:27:38.526
And it took me an entire year to finish.

00:27:38.526 --> 00:27:41.720
I remember when I finished it,

00:27:41.720 --> 00:27:44.370
was basically when I
graduated from university...

00:27:44.370 --> 00:27:45.203
- [Joey] Jesus.

00:27:45.203 --> 00:27:47.560
- And I put the script of this Top 20 list

00:27:47.560 --> 00:27:49.510
next to my dissertation.

00:27:49.510 --> 00:27:52.850
The top 20 list was twice
the length of my dissertation

00:27:52.850 --> 00:27:56.117
that I had worked my last year in uni on.

00:27:56.117 --> 00:27:57.717
- Hell, yeah.

00:27:57.717 --> 00:27:59.160
- So my dissertation,

00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:00.970
which I spent an entire year working on,

00:28:00.970 --> 00:28:04.970
was half the length of this
fucking YouTube video series

00:28:04.970 --> 00:28:06.627
that I'd worked on in that same year.

00:28:06.627 --> 00:28:07.580
- Oh my God.

00:28:07.580 --> 00:28:08.413
- So that was-

00:28:08.413 --> 00:28:09.246
- That's so good.

00:28:09.246 --> 00:28:10.983
- Yeah. At some point,

00:28:13.010 --> 00:28:15.960
it's not motivation
that's keeping you going,

00:28:15.960 --> 00:28:18.520
because when you have a project that big,

00:28:18.520 --> 00:28:19.580
you just wanna finish it

00:28:19.580 --> 00:28:21.410
just so you can fucking finish it.

00:28:21.410 --> 00:28:22.243
- Oh, yeah.

00:28:22.243 --> 00:28:23.076
- All through, you just wanna stop.

00:28:23.076 --> 00:28:23.909
- Yeah.

00:28:23.909 --> 00:28:24.742
- You can't; you've started.

00:28:24.742 --> 00:28:25.575
The Yaoi audiobook,

00:28:25.575 --> 00:28:30.340
which took me a month of probably
at least five days a week,

00:28:30.340 --> 00:28:33.150
eight to 12 hours nonstop.

00:28:33.150 --> 00:28:36.980
Reading this fucking book
over and over again nonstop.

00:28:36.980 --> 00:28:39.610
Read that book so many times, I hate it.

00:28:39.610 --> 00:28:40.840
I hate it now. I can't look at it.

00:28:40.840 --> 00:28:41.673
It drives me insane.

00:28:41.673 --> 00:28:43.940
I like it. I like it a lot, but I hate it.

00:28:43.940 --> 00:28:46.367
- 'Cause you get to about
50, 60% of the way in,

00:28:46.367 --> 00:28:47.526
and you're just like...

00:28:47.526 --> 00:28:48.359
- [Connor] I'm done.

00:28:48.359 --> 00:28:49.192
- This is shit. I'm done.

00:28:49.192 --> 00:28:50.025
I'm not doing this anymore.

00:28:50.025 --> 00:28:51.610
Then you're like, "But I gotta finish it."

00:28:51.610 --> 00:28:53.640
There's just something about

00:28:53.640 --> 00:28:57.220
having an unfinished project that just...

00:28:57.220 --> 00:28:59.102
- 50, 60% in, you can't stop.

00:28:59.102 --> 00:29:00.530
You have to.

00:29:00.530 --> 00:29:01.363
- People are gonna be like,

00:29:01.363 --> 00:29:02.970
"Oh, where's EvAbridged 2.0?"

00:29:02.970 --> 00:29:04.294
And I'm just like,

00:29:04.294 --> 00:29:05.349
"I did the first film.

00:29:05.349 --> 00:29:07.220
That, to me, is a completed project."

00:29:07.220 --> 00:29:10.410
Part of the big reason I
didn't wanna continue that

00:29:10.410 --> 00:29:13.350
was because I didn't wanna
put that upon myself again,

00:29:13.350 --> 00:29:14.357
to start a project that I knew

00:29:14.357 --> 00:29:16.373
was gonna take fucking years to finish.

00:29:17.521 --> 00:29:19.670
That's what excites me,

00:29:19.670 --> 00:29:22.640
but that's what also scares me the most,

00:29:22.640 --> 00:29:24.500
when it comes to taking on a big project.

00:29:24.500 --> 00:29:25.990
'Cause I've got a lot of different ideas

00:29:25.990 --> 00:29:28.280
for a lot of big projects
I eventually want to do.

00:29:28.280 --> 00:29:30.390
But just knowing what it's like,

00:29:30.390 --> 00:29:31.940
where you are excited,

00:29:31.940 --> 00:29:33.840
you're motivated for the first half,

00:29:33.840 --> 00:29:35.540
and then that just peters off

00:29:35.540 --> 00:29:38.080
and you start hating your project
and start hating yourself.

00:29:38.080 --> 00:29:38.927
And you're just like,

00:29:38.927 --> 00:29:40.242
"I just want to get this done."

00:29:40.242 --> 00:29:43.974
That to me is such an awful grind.

00:29:43.974 --> 00:29:46.040
- What about you, Joey?
What was your longest?

00:29:46.040 --> 00:29:46.950
- I don't know, I mean...

00:29:46.950 --> 00:29:49.916
- Is there a video that
stands out as being grueling?

00:29:49.916 --> 00:29:53.110
Or anything you worked
on music-wise, anything?

00:29:53.110 --> 00:29:55.220
- I mean, music-wise, I guess.

00:29:55.220 --> 00:29:57.215
My first album took me like two years.

00:29:57.215 --> 00:29:58.048
- Yeah 'cause how long

00:29:58.048 --> 00:29:59.260
were you working on that album for?

00:29:59.260 --> 00:30:01.330
- The first album, I took like two years.

00:30:01.330 --> 00:30:02.280
- [Connor] That's on-and-off, right?

00:30:02.280 --> 00:30:03.170
- [Joey] Yeah, that was on-and-off

00:30:03.170 --> 00:30:04.570
'cause that was just like a side project.

00:30:04.570 --> 00:30:07.014
- So you throw a little
bit here and there.

00:30:07.014 --> 00:30:07.880
- Yeah, whenever I felt like doing it,

00:30:07.880 --> 00:30:08.930
'cause it's not really,

00:30:08.930 --> 00:30:10.823
my career isn't dependent on my album.

00:30:10.823 --> 00:30:13.030
- When did you feel like it was ready

00:30:13.030 --> 00:30:14.603
to be released?

00:30:15.923 --> 00:30:17.765
Because I've had side projects like that,

00:30:17.765 --> 00:30:19.517
where you do a certain percentage

00:30:19.517 --> 00:30:21.376
and then you realize, "Wait a minute,

00:30:21.376 --> 00:30:23.163
I might actually get to the end of this.

00:30:23.163 --> 00:30:24.667
I might actually be able to finish this."

00:30:24.667 --> 00:30:26.090
- I mean, the first album
was like eight tracks

00:30:26.090 --> 00:30:28.447
and I think by track six, I was like,

00:30:28.447 --> 00:30:33.300
"Okay, is this enough for an
album or should I add more?"

00:30:33.300 --> 00:30:34.133
Not sure.

00:30:34.133 --> 00:30:38.210
Then after that, it was kind
of a rush of inspiration

00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:42.004
because it's you start
to see the final product.

00:30:42.004 --> 00:30:43.797
The goal is right there.

00:30:43.797 --> 00:30:45.383
I just need to run to it now.

00:30:46.595 --> 00:30:47.890
- The last 5% is actually really fun

00:30:47.890 --> 00:30:48.940
when it all starts to come together.

00:30:48.940 --> 00:30:50.080
- Yeah.

00:30:50.080 --> 00:30:51.380
The last 5% is like, "Hell, yeah."

00:30:51.380 --> 00:30:52.370
But I don't know.

00:30:52.370 --> 00:30:54.623
In terms of videos, not too sure.

00:30:54.623 --> 00:30:57.730
I think the reason why a lot
of my videos take so long

00:30:57.730 --> 00:31:01.550
is because either me, with
whatever I'm working with,

00:31:01.550 --> 00:31:03.640
takes a long time just come back to.

00:31:03.640 --> 00:31:04.950
A lot of it is just waiting.

00:31:04.950 --> 00:31:06.663
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah.

00:31:06.663 --> 00:31:08.110
- So I did that video with Ladybeard

00:31:08.110 --> 00:31:11.630
where we run around the figurine factory.

00:31:11.630 --> 00:31:12.700
When we did that video,

00:31:12.700 --> 00:31:14.410
that video took like eight months.

00:31:14.410 --> 00:31:16.674
- Oh god, counting time
just getting prepped,

00:31:16.674 --> 00:31:17.722
it's a different thing.

00:31:17.722 --> 00:31:19.860
- Tell me you're a Japanese YouTuber

00:31:19.860 --> 00:31:20.990
without telling me you're
a Japanese YouTuber.

00:31:20.990 --> 00:31:22.810
- That video took me eight months,

00:31:22.810 --> 00:31:23.780
but seven of those months

00:31:23.780 --> 00:31:26.150
was just waiting for
them to give me the okay

00:31:26.150 --> 00:31:27.740
and give me a good date to start.

00:31:27.740 --> 00:31:29.660
Then the actual shoot took
like a day and a half.

00:31:29.660 --> 00:31:32.470
So I feel like, in terms of just

00:31:32.470 --> 00:31:36.250
sheer working on a video time,

00:31:36.250 --> 00:31:38.930
maybe a month is max.

00:31:38.930 --> 00:31:40.500
I can't tell you which video it is,

00:31:40.500 --> 00:31:42.642
but I have a couple of videos like that.

00:31:42.642 --> 00:31:44.310
- I feel that with Trash
Taste specials there as well.

00:31:44.310 --> 00:31:45.329
- Oh yeah.

00:31:45.329 --> 00:31:46.323
- 'Cause like the lead...

00:31:46.323 --> 00:31:47.310
- The specials, I think, yeah,

00:31:47.310 --> 00:31:48.563
definitely the longest so far.

00:31:48.563 --> 00:31:50.980
- The lead time for the
specials is just so fucking long

00:31:50.980 --> 00:31:52.930
that sometimes you forget
that they're coming out.

00:31:52.930 --> 00:31:56.810
You're like, "Was this a good
special? I can't remember."

00:31:56.810 --> 00:31:59.310
I remember seeing the first draft

00:31:59.310 --> 00:32:01.210
of the drifting special
and the cycling special.

00:32:01.210 --> 00:32:02.577
I remember my first thought was,

00:32:02.577 --> 00:32:04.780
"God, I can't believe
I wasted all this time

00:32:04.780 --> 00:32:05.761
to record this shit."

00:32:05.761 --> 00:32:07.723
(all laughing)

00:32:07.723 --> 00:32:09.337
- By the time this episode comes out,

00:32:09.337 --> 00:32:11.160
the cooking special's probably out, right?

00:32:11.160 --> 00:32:12.200
- Yeah, it is.

00:32:12.200 --> 00:32:13.443
- I mean, I guess we can talk about that

00:32:13.443 --> 00:32:15.610
because that, oh my God,

00:32:15.610 --> 00:32:18.510
that first draft took like how long?

00:32:18.510 --> 00:32:22.220
- That's just because I think
it was one of those situations

00:32:22.220 --> 00:32:24.890
where Trash Taste takes priority.

00:32:24.890 --> 00:32:26.107
And because we're not,

00:32:26.107 --> 00:32:28.600
'cause we know people are willing to wait.

00:32:28.600 --> 00:32:29.433
It does take a while,

00:32:29.433 --> 00:32:31.530
'cause it's not prioritized at all.

00:32:31.530 --> 00:32:32.365
We don't say.

00:32:32.365 --> 00:32:34.255
- And I guess we do
want it to be the best.

00:32:34.255 --> 00:32:36.190
- Yeah, we don't mind making wait

00:32:36.190 --> 00:32:39.080
'cause so much work goes into the shoot.

00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:41.540
- It's the one thing I
don't want to compromise on

00:32:41.540 --> 00:32:43.240
in terms of quality.

00:32:43.240 --> 00:32:45.250
Can we talk about the Kendo special?

00:32:45.250 --> 00:32:46.760
- [Joey] I guess.
- [Connor] Sure.

00:32:46.760 --> 00:32:49.670
- Okay, so we released a picture

00:32:49.670 --> 00:32:51.970
of us filming a Kendo special.

00:32:51.970 --> 00:32:53.700
- [Connor] God, how fucking bad was that?

00:32:53.700 --> 00:32:56.300
- That was months and
months and months ago.

00:32:56.300 --> 00:32:58.727
A lot of viewers may have
just forgotten about it.

00:32:58.727 --> 00:33:01.218
But I know I see some Reddit
posts every now and again,

00:33:01.218 --> 00:33:02.530
bringing that special up.

00:33:02.530 --> 00:33:04.441
Like, "When's the Kendo special coming?"

00:33:04.441 --> 00:33:05.274
"When is it coming?"

00:33:05.274 --> 00:33:06.580
We actually scrapped the special

00:33:06.580 --> 00:33:10.480
because we filmed for an entire day.

00:33:10.480 --> 00:33:11.990
We got all the source footage

00:33:11.990 --> 00:33:14.780
and then Mudan edited a first draft

00:33:14.780 --> 00:33:16.350
and we thought it was shit.

00:33:16.350 --> 00:33:17.323
- It was shit.

00:33:17.323 --> 00:33:18.368
- And we thought,

00:33:18.368 --> 00:33:21.250
"There's only so much we can save

00:33:21.250 --> 00:33:22.860
through editing and voiceover,"

00:33:22.860 --> 00:33:23.890
'cause the source footage,

00:33:23.890 --> 00:33:25.940
unfortunately, just wasn't there.

00:33:25.940 --> 00:33:28.021
So we had to make the decision,

00:33:28.021 --> 00:33:30.630
"Do we try and maybe frame this,

00:33:30.630 --> 00:33:32.870
maybe release this as a mini-special

00:33:32.870 --> 00:33:35.480
or maybe something different?

00:33:35.480 --> 00:33:37.743
Maybe it goes in the After Dark channel?"

00:33:37.743 --> 00:33:39.630
But we eventually came to the decision

00:33:39.630 --> 00:33:41.860
that we spent an entire day filming.

00:33:41.860 --> 00:33:45.160
We hired three cameramen, four, maybe four

00:33:45.160 --> 00:33:46.960
and Ashley as a sound guy,

00:33:46.960 --> 00:33:50.230
we hired the Kendo people,
and we scrapped it.

00:33:50.230 --> 00:33:51.063
We just scrapped.

00:33:51.063 --> 00:33:53.000
