Every time I approach my car

01:45:48.330 --> 01:45:50.140
and it's just in a car park,

01:45:50.140 --> 01:45:51.640
could be empty, could be full.

01:45:52.520 --> 01:45:54.870
But I'm by myself and it's dark.

01:45:54.870 --> 01:45:56.870
First thing I have to
do, check the backseat.

01:45:56.870 --> 01:45:58.143
Make sure no one's in it.

01:45:58.143 --> 01:45:58.976
(Connor laughs)

01:45:58.976 --> 01:46:00.120
- Second thing I have to do,

01:46:00.120 --> 01:46:01.420
I have to go under

01:46:01.420 --> 01:46:03.890
and check that there's nobody
hiding underneath my car.

01:46:03.890 --> 01:46:05.246
- [Connor] Do you check that every time?

01:46:05.246 --> 01:46:06.396
- Like 90% of the time.

01:46:08.247 --> 01:46:09.080
- [Joey] Really?

01:46:09.080 --> 01:46:10.490
- I do it because I don't
feel safe unless I do it.

01:46:10.490 --> 01:46:12.250
- What's gonna be under your car?

01:46:12.250 --> 01:46:13.083
- [Garnt] Here's the reason.

01:46:13.083 --> 01:46:14.290
- A monster.

01:46:14.290 --> 01:46:15.550
- Here's the reason why.

01:46:15.550 --> 01:46:17.747
So when I was about, I can't remember,

01:46:17.747 --> 01:46:18.910
between five and seven.

01:46:18.910 --> 01:46:20.610
I think I was seven years old.

01:46:20.610 --> 01:46:22.917
I go to my cousin's house,
and of course, it's like,

01:46:22.917 --> 01:46:25.680
"Garnt, it's horror movie time again."

01:46:25.680 --> 01:46:27.343
I'm like, "No, please no."

01:46:27.343 --> 01:46:29.010
We're putting in the horror movie.

01:46:29.010 --> 01:46:30.907
This time, it's "Urban Legends".

01:46:31.894 --> 01:46:32.727
- Is it good?

01:46:32.727 --> 01:46:34.414
- I dunno if it's good.

01:46:34.414 --> 01:46:37.426
Scared the shit out of me as
a kid, I'll tell you that.

01:46:37.426 --> 01:46:38.259
- Oh yeah, I bet.

01:46:38.259 --> 01:46:39.623
- I've never watched it since.

01:46:40.650 --> 01:46:42.290
- You might get PTSD if you watch it now.

01:46:42.290 --> 01:46:43.123
- [Garnt] Honestly.

01:46:43.123 --> 01:46:44.160
- You will overcome your fear.

01:46:44.160 --> 01:46:44.993
- Well maybe, maybe.

01:46:44.993 --> 01:46:46.520
It's a slasher horror movie.

01:46:46.520 --> 01:46:48.070
So it was like '90s.

01:46:48.070 --> 01:46:49.533
So that's when slasher
horror movies were in.

01:46:49.533 --> 01:46:50.820
- [Connor] Like the "Scream" era.

01:46:50.820 --> 01:46:52.340
- Yeah. The "Scream" era.

01:46:52.340 --> 01:46:54.930
That's the horror movie
era that I grew up with

01:46:54.930 --> 01:46:57.590
and that's the kind of horror
movies that traumatized me.

01:46:57.590 --> 01:47:00.110
I remember

01:47:00.110 --> 01:47:01.250
it was this guy.

01:47:01.250 --> 01:47:03.907
I can't remember the exact
things that happened,

01:47:03.907 --> 01:47:06.150
but I remember it was surprise, surprise,

01:47:06.150 --> 01:47:08.330
about urban legends.

01:47:08.330 --> 01:47:10.720
You'd have these urban
legends that were spread out

01:47:10.720 --> 01:47:13.500
and sometimes these urban
legends would come true.

01:47:13.500 --> 01:47:16.300
I can't remember what the
exact urban legends were,

01:47:16.300 --> 01:47:17.800
but I remember this one scene.

01:47:18.978 --> 01:47:22.220
It was a guy who was
basically dressed up as Death

01:47:22.220 --> 01:47:23.220
and he had a scythe.

01:47:25.070 --> 01:47:27.230
I think part of the urban legend was

01:47:27.230 --> 01:47:29.700
that there would be this
guy in the back of your car

01:47:29.700 --> 01:47:31.160
while you're driving.

01:47:31.160 --> 01:47:32.450
This actually happened in the movie.

01:47:32.450 --> 01:47:34.060
There was this person driving the car

01:47:34.060 --> 01:47:35.070
and how he died was

01:47:35.070 --> 01:47:37.290
someone emerged from the back

01:47:37.290 --> 01:47:40.000
with a scythe and just
chopped him up to death.

01:47:40.000 --> 01:47:44.060
Of course, as a kid, that terrified me,

01:47:44.060 --> 01:47:46.177
'cause I remember thinking,

01:47:46.177 --> 01:47:48.360
"If I ever grow up and
get my driver's license,

01:47:48.360 --> 01:47:50.360
at any point in the dark,

01:47:50.360 --> 01:47:52.190
someone could come up from the back seat

01:47:52.190 --> 01:47:55.110
and stab me in the neck
or slice my neck open."

01:47:55.110 --> 01:47:56.720
- I kind of get that.

01:47:56.720 --> 01:48:01.720
- So that is just ingrained into my mind.

01:48:01.900 --> 01:48:03.870
But the second death in that movie,

01:48:03.870 --> 01:48:05.510
or it might be the third or the fourth,

01:48:05.510 --> 01:48:06.776
I can't remember.

01:48:06.776 --> 01:48:09.310
So this rumor gets spread around, right?

01:48:09.310 --> 01:48:11.187
That there's a guy in the backseat,

01:48:11.187 --> 01:48:13.000
there's a serial killer,

01:48:13.000 --> 01:48:14.650
and this is how this person died.

01:48:15.880 --> 01:48:17.130
So, of course, the fourth guy,

01:48:17.130 --> 01:48:18.620
he thinks he's better than this.

01:48:18.620 --> 01:48:19.820
He goes towards his car.

01:48:19.820 --> 01:48:22.180
He's a bit scared, but what does he do?

01:48:22.180 --> 01:48:23.450
He checks the backseat.

01:48:23.450 --> 01:48:25.096
Of course, he's like...

01:48:25.096 --> 01:48:26.547
- I've beat the system.

01:48:26.547 --> 01:48:29.070
- Ha. I beat the system. It's so dumb.

01:48:29.070 --> 01:48:32.820
Out of nowhere, the guy is
hiding underneath the car

01:48:32.820 --> 01:48:34.333
and slices his ankles.

01:48:35.695 --> 01:48:37.278
He starts crawling away.

01:48:37.278 --> 01:48:39.900
I remember this scene to this day.

01:48:39.900 --> 01:48:42.760
That's why, if I ever approach a car,

01:48:42.760 --> 01:48:44.240
I'm beating the system.

01:48:44.240 --> 01:48:45.230
First thing I'm doing,

01:48:45.230 --> 01:48:46.810
I'm checking underneath the car.

01:48:46.810 --> 01:48:48.040
Second thing I'm doing,

01:48:48.040 --> 01:48:50.786
I'm checking the backseat, right?

01:48:50.786 --> 01:48:52.290
There's no...

01:48:53.315 --> 01:48:54.327
- Then what if Death's like,

01:48:54.327 --> 01:48:57.110
"Big plot twist, passenger seat."

01:48:57.110 --> 01:48:58.830
- Look, look, look. If there's a sequel,

01:48:58.830 --> 01:49:00.240
if there's "Urban Legends 2",

01:49:00.240 --> 01:49:03.360
where someone adds on to this system,

01:49:03.360 --> 01:49:04.890
I'm fucked.

01:49:04.890 --> 01:49:05.723
- [Connor] Why?

01:49:05.723 --> 01:49:06.790
- But until then, I'm checking

01:49:06.790 --> 01:49:08.550
underneath every car I go to,

01:49:08.550 --> 01:49:10.630
and every backseat, if I'm by myself,

01:49:10.630 --> 01:49:11.870
'cause I'm not getting my ankles sliced.

01:49:11.870 --> 01:49:12.830
I'll tell you that much.

01:49:12.830 --> 01:49:15.260
- How did this man, not to nitpick,

01:49:15.260 --> 01:49:17.718
but how did he use a scythe in a car?

01:49:17.718 --> 01:49:18.696
- [Garnt] I don't know.

01:49:18.696 --> 01:49:19.666
- Was this like an SUV?

01:49:19.666 --> 01:49:20.499
- Mini-scythe.

01:49:20.499 --> 01:49:22.440
- This must have been a big scythe, man.

01:49:22.440 --> 01:49:24.650
You can't swing it in a car.

01:49:24.650 --> 01:49:26.840
The scythes are not short tools.

01:49:26.840 --> 01:49:29.043
Maybe a sickle, a sickle
might have worked.

01:49:29.043 --> 01:49:30.197
- I like how that's your
first question and not,

01:49:30.197 --> 01:49:31.340
"How did he get into the car?"

01:49:31.340 --> 01:49:33.705
- The first thing I was
thinking when he said this,

01:49:33.705 --> 01:49:35.870
I'm like, "How did this man
swing a scythe in a car?"

01:49:35.870 --> 01:49:38.150
I can barely swing my arms in a car.

01:49:38.150 --> 01:49:38.983
- That's a good question.

01:49:38.983 --> 01:49:40.434
I should have asked that as a kid.

01:49:40.434 --> 01:49:43.290
- Maybe if he kind of put it forward

01:49:43.290 --> 01:49:44.440
and then brought it backwards.

01:49:44.440 --> 01:49:46.180
But then how would you
slice it underneath?

01:49:46.180 --> 01:49:47.013
I feel like

01:49:47.997 --> 01:49:49.610
there's a lot of ways this could go wrong.

01:49:49.610 --> 01:49:52.160
- You're being a little
too realistic here.

01:49:52.160 --> 01:49:54.470
We first have to question,
"Why is Death in my car?"

01:49:54.470 --> 01:49:55.580
- That's why I'm like,

01:49:55.580 --> 01:49:58.410
I was gonna be scared
until the many plot holes

01:49:58.410 --> 01:49:59.340
that were available.

01:49:59.340 --> 01:50:00.560
I suddenly feel a lot safer.

01:50:00.560 --> 01:50:01.630
- Irrational.

01:50:01.630 --> 01:50:03.035
- I feel like, "This is good."

01:50:03.035 --> 01:50:04.100
- I feel like, as an adult,

01:50:04.100 --> 01:50:05.620
you can pick apart the plot holes

01:50:05.620 --> 01:50:06.670
in a lot of horror movies,

01:50:06.670 --> 01:50:08.240
and they stop being scary.

01:50:08.240 --> 01:50:09.310
- [Connor] That's true.

01:50:09.310 --> 01:50:11.700
- As a kid, you're like,
"(screaming) He's bleeding!

01:50:11.700 --> 01:50:13.800
He's bleeding! What the fuck?"

01:50:13.800 --> 01:50:16.520
- I get that backseat bullshit,

01:50:16.520 --> 01:50:18.520
because there's a lot of
Japanese horror films, as well,

01:50:18.520 --> 01:50:20.500
where that's very cliche.

01:50:20.500 --> 01:50:22.460
The other one that scares me is,

01:50:22.460 --> 01:50:24.360
and I hated this because my new place

01:50:24.360 --> 01:50:25.550
that I currently have has this,

01:50:25.550 --> 01:50:26.900
but in the bathroom,

01:50:26.900 --> 01:50:28.484
your mirror has a medicine cabinet.

01:50:28.484 --> 01:50:30.124
(Garnt laughing)

01:50:30.124 --> 01:50:32.500
- It's the thing of you're
brushing your teeth,

01:50:32.500 --> 01:50:34.990
and the medicine cabinet's slightly open,

01:50:34.990 --> 01:50:37.002
and then you close the medicine cabinet

01:50:37.002 --> 01:50:39.202
and then the monster
is standing behind you.

01:50:40.040 --> 01:50:42.120
Every now and then, I
have that thing where

01:50:42.120 --> 01:50:44.980
if I'm in the dark and the
medicine cabinet is open,

01:50:44.980 --> 01:50:47.704
before I close it, I just look behind me.

01:50:47.704 --> 01:50:48.537
- Do you actually?

01:50:48.537 --> 01:50:51.220
- Do you take a single
breath before you close?

01:50:51.220 --> 01:50:53.130
You're just like, "Okay."

01:50:53.130 --> 01:50:54.090
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:50:54.090 --> 01:50:55.584
I'm kind of like, I see it open.

01:50:55.584 --> 01:51:00.106
I'm like, (breathes out
forcefully) "Okay, I'm good.

01:51:00.106 --> 01:51:01.305
Okay guys, I'm good. Let's go."

01:51:01.305 --> 01:51:03.170
I get that every now and then.

01:51:03.170 --> 01:51:05.250
- I don't have any rituals like that

01:51:05.250 --> 01:51:09.830
to stop me from being scared
of something like that.

01:51:09.830 --> 01:51:10.663
- I don't know.

01:51:10.663 --> 01:51:12.960
I think to this day,

01:51:12.960 --> 01:51:14.977
there's some part about
me where it's like,

01:51:14.977 --> 01:51:16.980
"I'm still scared of the dark."

01:51:16.980 --> 01:51:17.813
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:51:17.813 --> 01:51:20.690
- For whatever bullshit reason.

01:51:20.690 --> 01:51:21.523
It's not because it's like,

01:51:21.523 --> 01:51:23.263
"I'm afraid of the guy behind me

01:51:23.263 --> 01:51:24.660
as I'm at the medicine
cabinet," or whatever,

01:51:24.660 --> 01:51:27.240
but it's like, in the back of your head,

01:51:27.240 --> 01:51:29.500
in the back of your fucked-up
imagination somewhere,

01:51:29.500 --> 01:51:31.870
you're like, "This is a possibility."

01:51:31.870 --> 01:51:34.450
- It's like when you're sleeping,

01:51:34.450 --> 01:51:36.830
and you're like, "Did
I leave my door open?"

01:51:36.830 --> 01:51:37.663
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:51:37.663 --> 01:51:38.496
- You know you didn't,

01:51:38.496 --> 01:51:39.570
but now you're gonna go check.

01:51:39.570 --> 01:51:40.428
- Yeah.

01:51:40.428 --> 01:51:41.261
- 'Cause you're like, "I thought I did,

01:51:41.261 --> 01:51:43.470
but I definitely didn't,
but I have to check."

01:51:43.470 --> 01:51:44.303
- Right, right, right, right.

01:51:44.303 --> 01:51:45.136
- It's kind of like that.

01:51:45.136 --> 01:51:46.460
Where you make yourself
think something is there.

01:51:46.460 --> 01:51:47.640
So now you have to check.

01:51:47.640 --> 01:51:48.473
- Exactly.

01:51:48.473 --> 01:51:49.704
- Otherwise you can't
stop thinking about it.

01:51:49.704 --> 01:51:50.922
I think I've had stuff like that with,

01:51:50.922 --> 01:51:52.240
"There could just be a monster

01:51:52.240 --> 01:51:54.533
on the other side of the
bed if I turn around.

01:51:54.533 --> 01:51:56.320
But I won't know unless I turn around.

01:51:56.320 --> 01:51:58.390
Guess I won't turn around."

01:51:58.390 --> 01:52:00.170
I have had thoughts like that.

01:52:00.170 --> 01:52:01.640
But I never actually like...

01:52:01.640 --> 01:52:02.580
- Put it into practice.

01:52:02.580 --> 01:52:04.800
- Even when I think, "Oh, I could just die

01:52:04.800 --> 01:52:07.517
if there was a guy standing
in my hallway with a knife."

01:52:07.517 --> 01:52:09.586
I don't actually think
that he's gonna be there,

01:52:09.586 --> 01:52:11.361
but I check.

01:52:11.361 --> 01:52:13.100
- You check just in case.

01:52:13.100 --> 01:52:15.610
- But I know there's no way
in hell someone's there.

01:52:15.610 --> 01:52:16.443
- Yeah.

01:52:16.443 --> 01:52:17.970
- But you just have to confirm it.

01:52:17.970 --> 01:52:20.000
I also get that every now and again,

01:52:20.000 --> 01:52:23.380
where it's the most irrational thoughts,

01:52:23.380 --> 01:52:26.030
where sometimes there's,

01:52:26.030 --> 01:52:27.747
you close the door and you're like,

01:52:27.747 --> 01:52:29.440
"Maybe there's a guy on the other side.

01:52:29.440 --> 01:52:31.420
Maybe there's someone
in my house right now."

01:52:31.420 --> 01:52:32.253
- [Joey] Yeah.

01:52:32.253 --> 01:52:33.086
- I don't know.

01:52:33.086 --> 01:52:34.760
Especially in the nighttime,

01:52:34.760 --> 01:52:38.280
and you hear something in
the middle of the night,

01:52:38.280 --> 01:52:39.840
in your living room or something.

01:52:39.840 --> 01:52:42.021
You're like, "I know
there's nothing in my house,

01:52:42.021 --> 01:52:42.854
(Joey laughs)

01:52:42.854 --> 01:52:43.687
- But what if?

01:52:43.687 --> 01:52:44.520
- What was that?

01:52:44.520 --> 01:52:45.977
- What if? I'm like,

01:52:45.977 --> 01:52:47.750
"I'm pretty sure there's
no ghosts in my house."

01:52:47.750 --> 01:52:49.722
I'm confident in my belief of ghosts

01:52:49.722 --> 01:52:52.010
that this place isn't haunted or whatever,

01:52:52.010 --> 01:52:53.630
even if there might be

01:52:53.630 --> 01:52:54.463
some haunted places in the world,

01:52:54.463 --> 01:52:56.273
but I'm pretty sure this
place isn't haunted,

01:52:56.273 --> 01:52:58.960
but then what the fuck was that noise?

01:52:58.960 --> 01:53:01.111
It could be the wind.
Definitely not the wind.

01:53:01.111 --> 01:53:02.112
No, definitely the wind.

01:53:02.112 --> 01:53:03.277
Definitely not the wind. Could be.

01:53:03.277 --> 01:53:05.490
You start second-guessing yourself.

01:53:05.490 --> 01:53:07.102
- Exactly. I feel that,

01:53:07.102 --> 01:53:10.190
especially recently with
some horror games I played,

01:53:10.190 --> 01:53:12.530
I feel that just resurfaced.

01:53:12.530 --> 01:53:15.740
It's not until you recently
consume content like that

01:53:15.740 --> 01:53:17.047
that you start to realize,

01:53:17.047 --> 01:53:20.030
"Oh, yeah. I think I'm
still afraid of this shit."

01:53:20.030 --> 01:53:22.301
I remember after I played
"P.T." for the first time,

01:53:22.301 --> 01:53:23.297
that made me so...

01:53:23.297 --> 01:53:26.610
I was like, "Hallways, lights on.

01:53:26.610 --> 01:53:30.450
Everywhere I go. I'm not
turning this shit off.

01:53:30.450 --> 01:53:31.881
Fuck that."

01:53:31.881 --> 01:53:33.001
(Garnt laughing)

01:53:33.001 --> 01:53:34.330
- It's so irrational.

01:53:34.330 --> 01:53:36.740
It's like, "Of course she's
not gonna be standing there

01:53:36.740 --> 01:53:37.665
at the end of the hallway."

01:53:37.665 --> 01:53:38.498
- Do you ever get the irrational fear

01:53:38.498 --> 01:53:41.080
that someone who's close
to you is not okay,

01:53:41.080 --> 01:53:42.600
and then you just text
them, like, "Are you okay?"

01:53:42.600 --> 01:53:43.433
(Joey laughing)

01:53:43.433 --> 01:53:44.266
- I get that. I get that.

01:53:44.266 --> 01:53:46.190
- You're like, "I had this weird dream.

01:53:46.190 --> 01:53:47.023
Just checking in that you're all right."

01:53:47.023 --> 01:53:49.960
- It's like, "You haven't
texted me in a while.

01:53:49.960 --> 01:53:51.240
We good? You good?"

01:53:51.240 --> 01:53:52.340
(Connor laughs)

01:53:52.340 --> 01:53:54.250
- Sometimes I'm just like,

01:53:54.250 --> 01:53:55.720
sometimes you go to a night out

01:53:55.720 --> 01:53:58.549
or hang out with someone,
and you're just like,

01:53:58.549 --> 01:54:01.640
"They said 10 words less
than what they usually said.

01:54:01.640 --> 01:54:03.027
Maybe there's something going on."

01:54:03.027 --> 01:54:05.683
- "They were blinking
a lot more than usual."

01:54:06.589 --> 01:54:08.850
- They were signaling something.

01:54:08.850 --> 01:54:10.148
- Morse code, maybe?

01:54:10.148 --> 01:54:12.080
(Joey laughs)

01:54:12.080 --> 01:54:12.913
- Oh my God.

01:54:14.010 --> 01:54:15.170
- I think part of the reason

01:54:15.170 --> 01:54:16.770
why I have so many lights on in my house

01:54:16.770 --> 01:54:19.150
is because of irrational fears like this.

01:54:19.150 --> 01:54:22.390
My mom would bollock me as a kid,

01:54:22.390 --> 01:54:24.750
'cause every time my mom
and dad would go out,

01:54:24.750 --> 01:54:27.000
they'd come home to a
house full of lights.

01:54:27.000 --> 01:54:31.003
They were like, "Garnt,
stop wasting electricity!"

01:54:32.210 --> 01:54:33.043
For the longest time,

01:54:33.043 --> 01:54:34.410
I think they just thought I would forget

01:54:34.410 --> 01:54:35.323
to turn off the lights.

01:54:35.323 --> 01:54:37.834
I never just told them, "No,
I'm just actually scared.

01:54:37.834 --> 01:54:39.690
But what if there's darkness?

01:54:39.690 --> 01:54:40.690
And what if there's something

01:54:40.690 --> 01:54:41.980
hiding in that darkness, Mom?

01:54:41.980 --> 01:54:45.420
You don't know. I'm in
this house by myself."

01:54:45.420 --> 01:54:46.713
